Linux-Networking-for-Devops


Network:
     A computer network formed when two or more computers are connected in some way, to share information or resources more broadly. 
     A network is the interconnection of computing devices, from computers, to phones, to printers to smart devices and so on


Network are typically made up of servers and clients:

Client-Server model: 
     This model, user devices or client, connect via to a network with centrally located server to get the resources they need.


A Server:
     is a large-capacity computer that contains the hard drives, printers and resources that are shared with other computers on a network
     server are designed to be able to handel more intensive workload that a personal computer can.Personal computer could run server process 
     but would not be able to handle the waste and crash


Client: 
     are other computers and devices on a network that request and receive resources from servers. Example end-user devices like phones 
     and personal computers

How does the client send a request to a server:
     Client side scripting enables interaction within a webpage... the code requried to process user input in downloaded and compiled  byby the browser 
     plugin

How does a server process a request:
     Server is a web application server at a remote location that will process web request and send pages to the client
     When a user goes to browser and types a webs... browser will search if website exist then asks server for specific page... server reacts by transferring files
     browser execute those files.

     A Client: A device or program that requires services via the web. Request the Server for content. The efficiency is limited. There are two or more clients.
     Server: A device or program that response by providing services. Provide function when client requests. There will be only one server. The power is high and 
     highlyefficient.

Web Server:
     A computer system that runs a website using HTTP, nginx, Apache... delivers content or web pages to end-users...
     Delivers STATIC files - HTML, CSS, 
     imagesHandles HTTP onlyIn
     Linux: nginx, apache2 listening on port 80/443
     Fast, does not run heavy code

Application Server: 
     is a Server program in a Computer in a distributed network that provides the business logic for an application example are 
     JBoss, oracle weblogic Server
     Runs BUSINESS LOGIC - login, payment, database queries
     Handles dynamic code - Java, Python, NodeIn 
     Linux: Tomcat, JBoss, gunicorn, pm2
     Example: When you click "Buy Now", web server forwards to app server

Server -> Physical Server / Virtual Server

Physical server: 
     is a dedicated Server, which use the traditional CPU and RAM for that one server

Virtual Server: 
     use hypervisor to divide the physical server into two or more virtual servers which share the resources like CPU and RAM

Private network:- 
     A private network excludes unauthorised users from joining network. An example is an intranet. A network where the connection is between 
     devices within a particular setting.

Public network:- 
     The public internet is also type of network. It is a global of other networks, allowing for worldwide sharing of information.
     Since it is accessible to public, the internet is an example public network.


